Chapter: LexStubs

 Outside the kernel there are no phase decks; the identity stub mirrors
 the one PlugTypes.codex carries for the same reason.

 deck-short-of asks whether the deck is within a guard band of a
 ceiling. With no deck there is no ceiling, and callers here pass 0,
 for which the real definition in Core/PhaseAllocator.codex returns
 False as well. It is written to stay loud rather than convenient: a
 caller that starts passing a real ceiling gets True, which empties the
 parse and shows up as a diff, instead of a quietly optimistic False.

Section: Stubs
  deck-record : a -> a
  deck-record (x) = x

  deck-short-of : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  deck-short-of (ceiling) (band) =
   if ceiling > 0 then True else False
